<title>USA: Italy's DINI says EMU not on G7 Denver agenda.</title>
<headline>Italy's DINI says EMU not on G7 Denver agenda.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Group of Seven industrialised nations are not expected to discuss the single European currency at their summit meeting starting later on Friday, Italian Foreign Minister Lamberto Dini said.</p>
<p>Dini, asked by reporters if European economic and monetary union (EMU) would be on the agenda, replied: &quot;I don't think so.&quot;</p>
<p>But Dini said he did not exclude the euro issue being discussed &quot;at finance minister level.&quot;</p>
</text>
